From 0d628228893817106f177004ff596c1e3efef6f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:09:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] ##arch: add PowerVR SGX Series-5 PDS data sequencer
 disassembler

Clean-room RArch plugin for the PDS (Programmable Data Sequencer) of the
PowerVR SGX Series-5 GPUs. The PDS runs the small programs that load
attributes and start USSE tasks; the SGX microkernel is entered through them.
Fixed 4-byte little-endian instructions: movs/movsa to the dout* issue ports,
mov16-mov128, load/store, integer ALU, tstz/tstn, bra/call/rtn/halt and fences,
with predicates. Op types and branch targets are set so analysis and graphs
work; targets are instruction indices from the start of the code.

The encoding was derived black-box from the reference PDS disassembler, used
only as an oracle; no vendor source is copied. It matches that oracle on the
SGX545 microkernel's five entry programs and on a 128k-word random corpus,
printing "invalid" only where the oracle reports a reserved encoding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
